  "doctrine": {
    "summary": "The PLA Ground Force is organised into combined-arms brigades (heavy, medium, light, amphibious, air assault) under five theatre commands, built around 'informatised' joint operations, massed precision rocket fires and heavy use of drones and electronic warfare. Training emphasis since 2015 is realistic opposed exercises, amphibious landings across the Taiwan Strait and high-altitude warfare on the Indian border. No large-scale combat since 1979; the 2020 Galwan clash was fought without firearms.",
    "squad_size": 10,
    "fireteam": "Rifle squad of ~10 (squad leader, deputy, LMG team, grenadier/PF-98 team, riflemen, DMR) in combined-arms brigades; game squads condensed to 8 in four battle-buddy pairs.",
    "tactics": [
      "Drill-perfect mounted assault: IFVs close under artillery and rocket fire, infantry dismounts late",
      "Massed precision fires from PHL-16/PCL-181 cued by drones before contact",
      "Heavy electronic warfare: jamming of radios and drone links is a constant map modifier",
      "Amphibious assault with ZBD-05 waves and Z-20/Z-10 air assault on coastal maps",
      "Mountain/high-altitude warfare with ZTQ-15 light tanks and Mengshi patrols",
      "Small-drone swarms and quadcopters for reconnaissance and grenade drops"
    ],
